{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetCBtQoJyhQyFCx9KzSU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Summary of Analysis:**\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a POST endpoint to confirm shipments, moving them from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, with idempotent retry support for already-confirmed shipments, and appropriate 404/409 errors for missing/cancelled shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment.kt:9-14 — Defines Shipment and ShipmentStatus (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController.kt:20-56 — Controller with create/getById/list, but no confirm endpoint\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27 — InMemoryShipmentRepository with save/findById/existsById\n- ApiExceptions.kt:18-24 — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 — ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n2. ErrorCode is a closed enum; all codes are defined centrally\n3. Tests assert on response body and error.code, not just status\n4. MockMvc tests verify state changes through separate GET requests\n5. State-changing endpoints return the modified entity\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Must add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code for cancelled shipments\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add 4 new tests covering all cases\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Breaking existing tests if unrelated changes are made\n2. Failing to verify state persistence through a separate GET (per testing-and-verification skill)\n3. Idempotent retry not working correctly\n4. Missing error.code assertions on negative cases\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum. This covers attempting to confirm a shipment that is in a state (e.g., CANCELLED) that does not permit confirmation.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new method annotated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Finds the shipment by ID, throwing ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves it\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) with the shipment in all success cases\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment` — POST confirm, verify 200 OK, separate GET verifies CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment is idempotent` — POST confirm twice, both succeed with same response, second GET verifies still CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm a CANCELLED shipment with 409 and error code` — POST confirm on cancelled, verify 409 and error.code, separate GET verifies still CANCELLED\n   - `confirm a non-existent shipment with 404` — POST confirm on missing ID, verify 404 and error.code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- **Reuse existing error code** — Could use SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for the cancelled case, but it's semantically wrong (shipment exists, it's not that). Adding a new code is clearer and follows the API contract principle.\n- **Not adding separate GET assertions** — The testing-and-verification skill makes clear that verifying through a second request is mandatory to ensure state actually persisted.\n- **Service layer abstraction** — Could create a ShipmentService with confirm logic, but the controller pattern already used in create() is sufficient and keeps changes minimal.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Processing | Output | Mechanism |\n|------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipmentId | Find shipment, verify status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save | 200 OK + updated Shipment | Controller calls repository.save(), returns ResponseEntity.ok() |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED (retry) | shipmentId | Find shipment, verify status is CONFIRMED, return unchanged | 200 OK + same Shipment | Controller returns the existing shipment unchanged |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId | Find shipment, verify status is CANCELLED, throw exception | 409 Conflict + error envelope | ConflictException caught by GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Confirm missing | invalid id | Find returns null, throw exception | 404 Not Found + error envelope | ResourceNotFoundException caught by GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test 1: Confirms a created shipment** — Create shipment (CREATED), POST confirm, assert 200 and shipment in body, separate GET /shipments/{id} asserts status is now CONFIRMED\n2. **Test 2: Confirm already-confirmed shipment is idempotent** — Create and confirm once, POST confirm again, assert 200 and same shipment body, second GET asserts status still CONFIRMED\n3. **Test 3: Confirm cancelled shipment returns 409 with error code** — Manually insert cancelled shipment in repository, POST confirm, assert 409 and error.code = SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, separate GET asserts still CANCELLED\n4. **Test 4: Confirm non-existent shipment returns 404** — POST confirm on missing ID, assert 404 and error.code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":22967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9bcba6c-6325-47f0-9e56-b214d796763d","uuid":"03d4c5b4-e5ff-45bb-89aa-a68943f47abe","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:38:18.886Z","request_id":"req_011CetCBsnM5DuZ91XJvLj1z"}
